  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n    [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (f : E → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)\n    (hf2 : MemLp f 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))\n    (hgrad2 : MemLp (gradient f) 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))\n    (hentropy : Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2))\n      (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) :\n    let γ : Measure E := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E\n    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤\n      2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient f x‖^2 ∂γ",
    "statement_sha256": "f905ed6ba2b029fec432b394b87220c134e2d54b5977d64b36fcb8f76cb11a16",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is any finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its compatible norm and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero.",
      "f is a signed real-valued function. ContDiff real 2 means globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E is literal canonical centered variance-one Gaussian measure, defined as the canonical orthonormal-basis map of the independent real Gaussian product.",
      "gradient is literal global Mathlib Riesz inverse applied to the real Frechet derivative. Norm is the Hilbert norm, not coordinate supremum or an arbitrary supplied representative.",
      "MemLp g 2 gamma means genuine AE strong measurability and finite L2 seminorm. Integrable h gamma means AE strong measurability and finite integral of its norm; no totalized integral fallback is intended.",
      "All displayed integrals are real Bochner integrals. Real.log is totalized at zero. The integrand t*log t is continuous including zero.",
      "The subtraction is homogeneous square entropy. No positive f, positive mass, compact support, normalization, supplied cutoff convergence or desired-inequality certificate is a premise."
    ]
  },
